# 7. P1 — MCP Runtime

## 7.1 MCP Supervisor

* [ ] MCP Server Registry
* [ ] MCP Connection Management
* [ ] MCP Discovery
* [ ] MCP Tool Discovery
* [ ] Heartbeat
* [ ] Automatic Reconnect
* [ ] Exponential Backoff
* [ ] Timeout
* [ ] Concurrent Calls
* [ ] Backpressure
* [ ] MCP Process Management

## 7.2 MCP Permissions

All MCP Tools must use the same Capability system:

```text
Agent
 ↓
MCP Supervisor
 ↓
Capability Check
 ↓
MCP Tool
 ↓
External Application
```

Example:

```text
Zeraix
 ↓
MCP
 ↓
Blender
```

MCP must not bypass Runtime Permission, Sandbox, or Audit mechanisms.

---

# 8. P1 — Context Management

## 8.1 Context Manager

* [ ] Context Budget
* [ ] Token Budget
* [ ] Context Priority
* [ ] Context Lifecycle
* [ ] Context Compaction
* [ ] Prefix Cache optimization
* [ ] Tool Result lifecycle management

## 8.2 Context Tiers

### CRITICAL

* User Goal
* Task Goal
* Current Plan
* Hard Constraints

### HIGH

* Important Decisions
* Important Facts
* Current Progress

### NORMAL

* Conversation Context
* Normal Model Output

### EPHEMERAL

* Tool Output
* Temporary Search Results
* Temporary Debug Information

## 8.3 Compaction

When Context approaches its budget:

```text
Context
  ↓
Budget Check
  ↓
Compaction
  ↓
Preserve CRITICAL
  ↓
Preserve HIGH
  ↓
Compress NORMAL
  ↓
Remove EPHEMERAL
```

### Critical Requirement

Compaction must preserve:

* [ ] User Goal
* [ ] Current Plan
* [ ] Current Phase
* [ ] Completed Tasks
* [ ] Pending Tasks
* [ ] Important Decisions
* [ ] Important Constraints

The Agent must not lose its task state after compaction.

